# Local secrets for the vps/ scripts. Copy to vps/.env and fill in.
#   cp vps/.env.example vps/.env
#
# vps/.env is gitignored. relay.sh and local-ports.sh source it automatically
# (each looks for .env next to itself) — no separate `source` step needed.

# relay.sh — forwards a public VPS port to a service on ANOTHER tailnet host
# (e.g. Plex on the home server), reached over Tailscale.
#
# Tailnet IP of the host actually running the service — required, e.g. the
# home server's `tailscale ip -4`. NOT this VPS's own tailnet IP.
TARGET_IP=

# Comma-separated list of ports to relay. Each entry:
#   PORT                    same public and target port, TCP
#   PUBLIC:TARGET           different public vs. target port, TCP
#   PORT/udp                UDP instead of TCP
#   PORT/tcp+udp            both protocols
#   PUBLIC:TARGET/tcp+udp   combine both
# Defaults to "32400" (Plex) if left unset. Removing a port from this list and
# re-running the script CLOSES it (also remember to delete its OCI ingress rule).
# Example: RELAY_PORTS=32400,8080:9090,51820/udp
RELAY_PORTS=32400/tcp+udp

# local-ports.sh — opens a public port for a service running ON THIS VPS
# ITSELF — no relay/forwarding, traffic terminates here.
#
# Comma-separated list of ports, same PORT[/tcp|udp|tcp+udp] syntax as
# RELAY_PORTS above (no PUBLIC:TARGET form — there's only one port, it's
# local). Leave empty/unset if this VPS has nothing running locally to expose.
# Example: LOCAL_PORTS=8080,3000/tcp+udp
LOCAL_PORTS=8080/tcp+udp
